OL,3,A'Slim chance' government will hit 1.5m
OL,4,Anew homes target, Rayner tells BBC
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere is only a "slim chance" the
OL,7,Fgovernment will meet its target of
OL,8,Fbuilding 1.5 million homes in England
OL,9,Fby the next election, Housing Secretary
OL,10,FAngela Rayner has told the BBC.
OL,12,F"Headwinds" including the Iran war and
OL,13,Frising construction costs are making it
OL,14,Fharder to meet the key Labour manifesto
OL,15,Fpledge, Rayner told the BBC's Sunday
OL,16,Fwith Laura Kuenssberg.
OL,18,F"But I'm definitely not giving it up,"
OL,19,Fshe said, and stressed that the
OL,20,Fgovernment was "making a difference"
OL,21,Fthrough investing billions in social
OL,22,Fand affordable homes.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
